# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KickTech HumanBadge — public repo .gitignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the PUBLIC mirror of the HumanBadge extension. The public repo
# is a curated subset of the private development repo. The patterns below
# are defensive guards: most should never appear here, but if they did,
# we want git to refuse to track them. The complement to this file is
# the publish-scope CI workflow in .github/workflows/publish-scope.yml,
# which actively rejects pushes containing disallowed paths.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── OS metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__MACOSX/
._*
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ── Editor / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
*#
.*.un~
.netrwhist
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# ── Source & build infra that belongs to the private repo only ──────────
# These should NEVER be in the public repo. The CI workflow rejects
# pushes that introduce them; this is a second line of defense.
src/
scripts/
.dev/
.private/
*.local
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Secrets / credentials (none should exist here, defensive) ──────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
.secrets/

# ── Temporary / backup / build artifacts ───────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
*.log
.cache/
build/
out/
tmp/
temp/

# ── Coverage / test output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# ── Override global .gitignore — dist/ IS our published artifact ───────
# Some developers have `dist/` in ~/.gitignore_global because for most
# projects dist/ is build output. In this public-mirror repository, dist/
# is the primary published artifact — every file in dist/ MUST be tracked.
!dist/
!dist/**
